// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`designToMarkdown > renders the example fixture 1`] = `
"# Churn Prediction (Telecom)

_ML System Architecture Spec_

## 1. Problem Space

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Domain | Telecom (Prepaid) |
| Business Goal | Reduce churn by 5% |
| ML Task | Binary classification |
| Constraints | Fixed discount budget |
| Horizon | 30 days |

Prepaid subscribers can leave at any time without notice. Retention offers cost money, so the model must rank who to target within a fixed budget.

## 2. Evaluation (Offline)

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Offline Metric | Precision@Top-10% |
| Loss | LogLoss |
| Target Value | > 0.35 |

The retention team can only call the top decile, so precision in that slice matters more than global AUC.

**Trade-off Matrix**

| Option | Matches business action | Stable on imbalance |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ✅ Precision@Top-10% (chosen) | Yes | Yes |
| ROC AUC | No, global ranking | Yes |
| Accuracy | No | No, 95% trivial |

## 3. Baseline

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Approach | Rule-based |
| Baseline Metric | 12.4% Prec@Top-10% |

Rules on tenure and recent top-ups are what the retention team uses today, so they are the bar to beat.

**Trade-off Matrix**

| Option | Cost | Time to ship |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ✅ Rules (chosen) | Low | 1 week |
| Logistic Regression | Low | 3 weeks |

## 4. Validation

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Strategy | OOT Split |

Train on 12 months, validate on the following month to mimic production drift.

![Validation diagram](images/validation.svg)

## 5. Data & Features

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Sources | CRM, Clicks |
| Key Features | Usage, Demographics, Network |
| Volume | 50M/mo |

Usage aggregates over 7/30/90 days carry most of the signal.

- Usage features
- Demographics
- Network quality

## 6. Evaluation (Online)

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Evaluation Type | A/B test, 10% |
| Key Metric | -2% churn |

A 10% holdout gives enough power to detect a 2% churn change in four weeks.

## 7. Integration

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Inference Pattern | Batch Inference |
| Output | Redis Cache |
| Latency Budget | Nightly, < 2h |

Offers are sent once a day, so nightly batch scoring is enough.

**Trade-off Matrix**

| Option | Cost | Freshness |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ✅ Batch (chosen) | Low | Daily |
| Streaming | High | Minutes |

## 8. Monitoring

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Data Drift | PSI < 0.2 |
| Model Quality | Weekly Prec@Top-10% |
| Alerting | Slack on breach |

Labels arrive with a 30-day delay, so input drift is the early signal.

## 9. Target Solution & Architecture

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Model Type | Gradient Boosted Machine |
| Algorithm | XGBoost Classifier |
| Environment | Python / Kubernetes |

Gradient boosting handles tabular, mixed-type features well and is cheap to serve in batch.

**Trade-off Matrix**

| Option | Accuracy | Explainability | Training cost |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| ✅ XGBoost (chosen) | High | SHAP | Low |
| Neural net | High | Weak | High |
| Logistic Regression | Medium | Native | Low |

![Target Solution & Architecture diagram](images/target-solution.svg)
"
`;
